  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to exert its biological effects through a shared mechanism involving Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which acts as a target of multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Oblonganoside C targets Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which in turn targets SK-LU-1, a cancer cell line. This relationship is supported by multiple high-scoring pathways, with scores ranging from 0.6121 to 0.6484, indicating a consistent and plausible interaction. The core mechanism involves Ent-Gloeosteretriol acting as a mediator, potentially modulating cellular processes that lead to the suppression of SK-LU-1. The presence of multiple independent pathways reinforcing this relationship strengthens the hypothesis that Oblonganoside C may influence SK-LU-1 through Ent-Gloeosteretriol. The integration of these pathways supports a mechanistic link, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact role of Ent-Gloeosteretriol in this context.",
